comprehensive-documentation-engineering — licensing
====================================================

This package is dual-licensed by file, because it combines original work with
adaptations of material published under CC BY-SA 4.0. A skill built on someone
else's methodology inherits that methodology's license wherever it reproduces
the methodology's text.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. CC BY-SA 4.0 — reference sheets adapting Diátaxis doctrine
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The following files adapt content from Diátaxis (https://diataxis.fr),
copyright (c) Daniele Procida, licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). Under the ShareAlike
condition these adaptations are also licensed CC BY-SA 4.0, and each file
carries an attribution header naming its source pages and the changes made:

  references/diataxis-foundations.md
  references/compass-and-classification.md
  references/tutorials.md
  references/how-to-guides.md
  references/reference.md
  references/explanation.md
  references/anti-patterns.md                 (Diátaxis-derived portions)
  references/information-architecture.md       (complex-hierarchies portions)
  references/style-overrides.md                (per-quadrant "default" portion)
  references/accessibility-and-localization.md (translation-practice portion)

references/diagrams.md additionally describes the C4 model by Simon Brown
(https://c4model.com), whose content is licensed CC BY 4.0; that material is
attributed in the file's header. The remainder of diagrams.md is MIT.

